From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add Korean multibyte text core smoke path

Reference: pret/pokeemerald @ 5eff78649e7170a877b961ef0b3da13b81a16038

Introduce a non-colliding printable token FC 19 LL HH. LL/HH encode one
supported Korean BMP code point in little-endian order. Existing Latin,
Japanese, CHAR_DYNAMIC, keypad, extra-symbol and control encodings remain
unchanged.

This first executable slice embeds four byte-exact Korean SoulSilver MESSAGE
font glyphs (가나다라) as a smoke fixture. It proves the 16x16/64-byte glyph
path without pretending that the full 11,172-glyph asset pack has already
been integrated. Unsupported Korean code points fall back to the stock
question-mark glyph.

diff --git a/include/constants/characters.h b/include/constants/characters.h
--- a/include/constants/characters.h
+++ b/include/constants/characters.h
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@
 #define EXT_CTRL_CODE_ENG                    0x16
 #define EXT_CTRL_CODE_PAUSE_MUSIC            0x17
 #define EXT_CTRL_CODE_RESUME_MUSIC           0x18
+#define EXT_CTRL_CODE_KOREAN_GLYPH           0x19 // FC 19 LL HH; Unicode BMP code point, little-endian
 
